A _dielectric_ describes a medium which does not completely screen an external macroscopic electric field $va(E)_"ext"$ from its interior.

A dielectric---similar to the conducting case---subject to the influence of such an external field, will rearrange its charge distribution in such a way that a field $va(E)_"self"$ is produced, but insofar that
$
  va(E)_"tot" = va(E)_"ext" + va(E)_"self" = 0.
$
The chemical bonding effects give rise to local maxima and minima in the potential landscape that inhibit the electron wavefunctions from propagating.
